  "Discord 把訊息依頻道（和時間區段）分到資料庫的分割區；一個超大伺服器在發公告時，所有人讀同一個頻道，這個分割區所在的節點就變成熱點，連帶拖慢同節點上的其他查詢。這個模型用 8 個分片和很集中的 key，看一個分片忙到滿、其他分片很閒。": "Discord splits messages into database partitions by channel (and time range); when a very large server posts an announcement, everyone reads the same channel, so the node that holds that partition becomes a hot spot and slows other queries on the same node. This model uses 8 shards with very concentrated keys, so one shard stays fully busy while the others sit idle.",
  "DocDB proxy（依 chunk 路由）": "DocDB proxy (routes by chunk)",
  "DocDB（分片，每片 1 主 2 副本）": "DocDB (sharded, 1 primary + 2 replicas each)",
  "Dropbox 的 ATF 讓各團隊排程背景任務：前端收到請求寫進任務儲存，再經佇列交給 executor 執行，保證至少執行一次。這個模型的上傳 API 同步寫物件儲存，再丟任務到佇列；executor 處理後寫回資料庫。重點是：同步路徑上的依賴變慢，會卡住前台；非同步路徑變慢只會讓任務晚一點完成。": "Dropbox's ATF lets teams schedule background jobs: the front end receives a request, writes it to job storage, then hands it to an executor through a queue with at-least-once execution. In this model the upload API writes to object storage synchronously, then puts a job on the queue; the executor processes it and writes back to the database. The point: a slow dependency on the sync path blocks the front end; a slow async path only makes the job finish later.",
