  "FIFO {id}：{n} 則訊息排在同組前一則後面等": "FIFO {id}: {n} messages waited behind an earlier message of their group",
  "FIFO 時，訊息依 key 分成幾組（像 message group 或 partition 數）。組越少，越容易互相卡住；也限制同時能處理的訊息數。": "With FIFO, messages are split into this many groups by key (like message groups or partitions). Fewer groups block each other more often, and also limit how many messages are worked on at once.",
  "FIFO（像 SQS FIFO、Kafka 的 partition）：同一組（同一個 key）的訊息一次只交出一則，前一則做完、失敗丟掉或進 DLQ 才交下一則。前一則卡住（處理很慢、毒訊息一直重試），後面整組都等（head-of-line blocking）。": "FIFO (like SQS FIFO or a Kafka partition): messages of one group (one key) are handed out one at a time; the next one goes only when the previous one is done, dropped or moved to the DLQ. When one is stuck (slow, or a poison message retried again and again), its whole group waits (head-of-line blocking).",
  "FIFO（同一組依序）": "FIFO (in order per group)",
  "FIFO：同一組前一則還沒做完，這則只能等（head-of-line blocking）": "FIFO: messages that waited because an earlier one of their group was not done (head-of-line blocking)",
