  "Instagram 2011：Django＋分片 PostgreSQL＋Memcached": "Instagram 2011: Django + sharded PostgreSQL + Memcached",
  "Instagram App（API）": "Instagram app (API)",
  "Instagram 上線一年後（2011 年，1,400 萬用戶、3 個工程師）的整套架構。App 的請求經 Route53 → Amazon ELB（在這裡終結 SSL）→ 3 台 NGINX → 25 台以上的 Django（gunicorn）。大部分資料（用戶、照片資訊、tag）放在分片的 PostgreSQL：12 台主庫，另一個可用區有 12 台副本，用串流複製。前面有 6 台 Memcached。Redis 存首頁 feed、動態、session。地理搜尋改用 Apache Solr。照片直接存 S3，用 CloudFront 當 CDN。分享到 Twitter／Facebook、通知訂閱者、feed 的 fan-out 都丟進 Gearman 佇列，約 200 個 Python worker 在背景處理；推播用 pyapns。來源：https://instagram-engineering.com/what-powers-instagram-hundreds-of-instances-dozens-of-technologies-adf2e22da2ad 、https://instagram-engineering.com/sharding-ids-at-instagram-1cf5a71e5a5c 。lease 的作法出自 Facebook 的論文 Scaling Memcache at Facebook（NSDI 2013）：https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi13/technical-sessions/presentation/nishtala 。參數是教學用的縮小值，不是 Instagram 的實際數字。": "The whole architecture of Instagram one year after launch (2011: 14 million users, 3 engineers). App requests go through Route53 → Amazon ELB (SSL terminates here) → 3 NGINX servers → 25+ Django (gunicorn) servers. Most data (users, photo metadata, tags) is in sharded PostgreSQL: 12 primaries, with 12 replicas in another availability zone through streaming replication. 6 Memcached servers are in front. Redis holds the home feed, the activity feed and sessions. Geo search moved to Apache Solr. Photos go straight to S3, with CloudFront as the CDN. Sharing to Twitter/Facebook, notifying followers and feed fan-out go on a Gearman queue, and about 200 Python workers process them in the background; push notifications use pyapns. Sources: https://instagram-engineering.com/what-powers-instagram-hundreds-of-instances-dozens-of-technologies-adf2e22da2ad , https://instagram-engineering.com/sharding-ids-at-instagram-1cf5a71e5a5c . The lease approach comes from Facebook's paper Scaling Memcache at Facebook (NSDI 2013): https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi13/technical-sessions/presentation/nishtala . The parameters are small values for teaching, not Instagram's real numbers.",
  "Instagram 的資料主要放在 PostgreSQL（一個主庫、各區域有副本），前面用 memcache 擋讀取。當快取被清空或失效，所有 Django 伺服器同時去查資料庫（thundering herd），他們用 memcache lease 解決。這個模型讓快取停 5 秒，恢復後是冷的，看資料庫副本被灌爆。": "Instagram keeps most data in PostgreSQL (one primary, a replica in each region) and puts memcache in front to absorb reads. When the cache is flushed or expires, all Django servers query the database at once (thundering herd); they solved this with a memcache lease. This model stops the cache for 5 s; it comes back cold, and you can watch the database replicas get flooded.",
  "JQRelay（Kafka → Redis）": "JQRelay (Kafka → Redis)",
